  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 720.08 Qualifications of Level 1 Assessors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 720.08 Qualifications of Level 1 Assessors.\n\n(a) A PWS owner shall ensure that each individual performing a level 1 assessment is familiar with the operation and management of the PWS to be assessed.\n\n(b) A level 1 assessment shall be conducted by:\n\n(1) For transient, non-community water systems (NCWSs), the owner or the owner’s authorized agent;\n\n(2) For non-transient, non-community systems (NTNCWSs), the owner, the owner’s authorized agent, or an operator certified at a grade comparable to or higher than the required grade for that PWS; and\n\n(3) For community water systems (CWSs), an operator certified at a grade comparable to or higher than the required grade for that system.\n\nSource. #9760, eff 7-30-10; ss by #10771, eff 2-1-15; ss by #14427, eff 11-21-25, EXPIRES 11-21-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
